# Deploy and ops

Contract: `../scaleway-push-template.md`. Commands: `scripts/push_*.sh` (they print server steps).

## Principles

**Build elsewhere, run elsewhere.** Images are produced and pushed from dev/CI; servers pull, pin, and recreate—never compile app images on production hosts.

**Immutable releases.** Prefer digest or content-addressed tags over floating `:latest` for anything operators depend on.

**Config is layered.** Compose and proxy files sync when they change; secrets live in server `.env`—merge new keys from `.env.example`, don’t blindly overwrite production secrets.

**Schema follows code.** Backend releases that change models require migration to head in the running `app` container before you treat deploy as complete.

**One-time vs recurring.** Infrastructure bootstrap (RAG role, seed SQL) is volume-lifetime; migrations and image rollouts are per release. Don’t repeat bootstrap rituals every push.

**Verify behavior, not just health.** Use repo verify scripts that exercise gateway consumer paths and core API flows—not only `docker compose ps`.

**Dependency order.** External gateway before LAED before dependent siblings on cold boot.

Sensitive proxy auth material stays out of compose `.env` files that break on interpolation—follow the repo’s split-env pattern.
